ng\n                        material; never uploads\n    publish-verify-export\n                        Prepare and inspect offline chapter publishing\n                        material; never uploads\n    workbench-snapshot  Read one bounded, non-mutating local workbench\n                        snapshot\n    workbench-export    Generate a self-contained, read-only local author\n                        workbench\n    workbench-serve     Open a loopback editor that saves candidate drafts\n                        only\n    workbench-status    Check the registered local editor instance\n    workbench-stop      Stop the registered editor after preserving edits in\n                        all its pages\n    workbench-library-serve\n                        Open the independent local bookshelf at a fixed\n                        address\n    workbench-library-status\n                        Check the independent bookshelf service\n    workbench-library-stop\n                        Stop the bookshelf without stopping book editors\n    export              Repair exports without replacing outside edits\n    assemble-short      Assemble all committed short-story chapters into one\n                        book-title Markdown file\n    notes               Save cards or a chapter plan with optimistic\n                        concurrency\n    plan                Save cards or a chapter plan with optimistic\n                        concurrency\n    plan-read           Read a complete saved chapter plan for recovery\n                        without verifying adoption\n    outline-bind        Bind one reviewed, adopted readable outline to its\n                        saved chapter plan\n    context             Build a bounded chapter context packet\n    prepare             Read-only review scaffold bound to the current book,\n                        state and draft\n    reconcile           Inspect an outside edit of the latest native chapter,\n                        or apply its re